final-link wall
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
symbol 'foo' is called but has no linked body
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Check that goto-cc --export-file-local-symbols at link time warns
when a function body is missing in the linked binary but its name
is called from another body.  LIM-009 in integration/linux/CBMC_
LIMITATIONS.md is the concrete motivator: a kernel `static` symbol
bound to an empty external stub because the caller's `extern`
declaration used the unmangled name.  Without this warning CBMC
silently treats the call as nondet-return.  Here, `foo` is
`static` in foo.c and gets mangled to
`__CPROVER_file_local_foo_c_foo`; main.c's unmangled `extern int
foo(void)` therefore has no linked body at final-link time.
